# fix symmetry example: binary LJ alloy with L1_2 (Cu3Au) structure and
# inversion symmetry (space group P-1)
#
# The FCC lattice with the corner atoms of each cubic unit cell as type 2
# and the face centered atoms as type 1.  Inversion through the origin of
# the box maps each type onto itself, as required: fix symmetry stops
# with an error if an atom and its image have different types.

units           lj
atom_style      atomic

lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box basis 1 2
mass            * 1.0

pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 0.5 0.9
pair_coeff      1 2 0.7 0.95
pair_modify     shift yes
neighbor        0.3 bin

fix             1 all nve
fix             sym all symmetry p-1.json

velocity        all create 1.0 87287 loop geom
run             0 post no
velocity        all scale 1.0

variable        odd atom sin(2*PI*(x-xlo)/lx)+sin(2*PI*(y-ylo)/ly)+sin(2*PI*(z-zlo)/lz)
compute         odd all reduce sum v_odd

thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press c_odd
thermo          100
run             1000
